meta {
  name: tag: gatus tapis-actors postgres (stack)
  type: http
  seq: 24
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/pods/templates/gatus/tags
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-Tapis-Token: {{X-Tapis-Token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "kind": "stack",
    "stack_definition": {
      "restart_policy": "ordered",
      "secret_map": {
        "PG_PASSWORD": "${pods:random:32}",
        "TAPIS_USERNAME": "${:?Tapis username for minting the X-Tapis-Token (NOT a service account)}",
        "TAPIS_PASSWORD": "${:?Password for TAPIS_USERNAME}",
        "TAPIS_CLIENT_BASIC": "${:?base64 of 'client_id:client_key' for the password grant. The Tapis password grant REQUIRES a registered OAuth client; create one with POST /v3/oauth2/clients, then base64-encode client_id:client_key. A gatus config cannot omit the Basic auth header conditionally, so this is required here.}"
      },
      "members": [
        {
          "name": "db",
          "image": "postgres:17-alpine",
          "description": "Postgres 17 for gatus actors-watch history, backed by a tapisvolume so the large backlog survives even a db-pod recreation. local_only - never exposed outside the cluster.",
          "ready_condition": "ready",
          "time_to_stop_default": -1,
          "networking": {
            "default": {
              "protocol": "local_only",
              "port": 5432,
              "tapis_auth": false
            }
          },
          "healthchecks": {
            "readiness": {
              "exec_command": [
                "pg_isready",
                "-U",
                "gatus",
                "-d",
                "gatus"
              ],
              "initial_delay_seconds": 5,
              "period_seconds": 5
            },
            "networking_requires_ready": false
          },
          "environment_variables": {
            "POSTGRES_DB": "gatus",
            "POSTGRES_USER": "gatus",
            "POSTGRES_PASSWORD": "${stack:secrets:PG_PASSWORD}",
            "PGDATA": "/var/lib/postgresql/data/pgdata"
          },
          "volume_mounts": {
            "/var/lib/postgresql/data": {
              "type": "tapisvolume",
              "source_id": "${:?Tapis volume ID for durable Postgres data (create one first: POST /v3/pods/volumes). PGDATA lives in the /pgdata subdir so the mount root can hold lost+found.}"
            }
          },
          "resources": {
            "cpu_request": 250,
            "cpu_limit": 2000,
            "mem_request": 256,
            "mem_limit": 2048
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "app",
          "image": "twinproduction/gatus:v5.36.0",
          "description": "Gatus v5.36.0 running the tapis-actors-suite (in-suite X-Tapis-Token mint + 3-minute /v3/actors watch) with postgres storage and a large retention backlog. Actor creds + DB password reach gatus via ENV, never the rendered config.",
          "depends_on": [
            "db"
          ],
          "time_to_stop_default": -1,
          "environment_variables": {
            "TAPIS_BASE_URL": "https://tacc.tapis.io",
            "TAPIS_USERNAME": "${stack:secrets:TAPIS_USERNAME}",
            "TAPIS_PASSWORD": "${stack:secrets:TAPIS_PASSWORD}",
            "TAPIS_CLIENT_BASIC": "${stack:secrets:TAPIS_CLIENT_BASIC}",
            "GATUS_DB_HOST": "${stack:db:host}",
            "GATUS_DB_PORT": "5432",
            "GATUS_DB_USER": "gatus",
            "GATUS_DB_NAME": "gatus",
            "GATUS_DB_PASSWORD": "${stack:secrets:PG_PASSWORD}"
          },
          "volume_mounts": {
            "/config/config.yaml": {
              "type": "ephemeral",
              "read_only": false,
              "config_permissions": "0644",
              "config_filename": "config.yaml",
              "config_update_mode": "always",
              "config_content": "# ============================================================================\n# Tapis Abaco actors watch (postgres) - durable, large-backlog version of the\n# gatus:tapis-actors-suite tag. Mints an X-Tapis-Token in-suite, then polls\n# /v3/actors every 3 minutes to catch rapid GET changes.\n#\n# What changed vs the memory-storage suite tag:\n#   * storage.type: postgres  -> check history survives app restarts/upgrades\n#   * maximum-number-of-*      -> a large retention backlog (see notes below)\n#\n# Secrets (TAPIS_USERNAME / TAPIS_PASSWORD / TAPIS_CLIENT_BASIC) are expanded by\n# gatus itself from the pod ENV (${VAR}) - sourced from stack secrets - so they\n# live only in the k8s secret, never in the rendered config file. GATUS_DB_*\n# reach storage.path the same way. key=value DSN (not postgres://) because\n# ${pods:random:32} can emit @ # % which corrupt a URL.\n# ============================================================================\n\nmetrics: true\n\nstorage:\n  type: postgres\n  path: \"host=${GATUS_DB_HOST} port=${GATUS_DB_PORT} user=${GATUS_DB_USER} password='${GATUS_DB_PASSWORD}' dbname=${GATUS_DB_NAME} sslmode=disable\"\n  # --- large history backlog ---------------------------------------------\n  # Retention is COUNT-based, not time-based. Wall-clock history per endpoint\n  # = maximum-number-of-results x interval. At the 3m suite cadence:\n  #   10000 results  ~= 20.8 days of per-result history per endpoint.\n  # To cover more calendar time, prefer raising `interval` over this cap -\n  # a higher row count costs DB size + dashboard query time on every load.\n  maximum-number-of-results: 10000\n  # Events are UP<->DOWN transitions only (rare), so 1000 spans many months.\n  maximum-number-of-events: 1000\n\nweb:\n  port: 8080\n\nui:\n  title: \"Tapis Actors Watch\"\n  header: \"Abaco /v3/actors - token-minted suite (durable)\"\n\nconcurrency: 3\n\nsuites:\n  - name: abaco-actors-watch\n    group: tapis\n    interval: 3m          # tight cadence to surface rapid GET changes; drop to 1m for a hot loop\n    timeout: 30s\n    endpoints:\n      # 1) Mint an X-Tapis-Token (password grant). Stored as `tapis_token`.\n      - name: mint-tapis-token\n        url: \"${TAPIS_BASE_URL}/v3/oauth2/tokens\"\n        method: POST\n        headers:\n          Content-Type: \"application/json\"\n          Authorization: \"Basic ${TAPIS_CLIENT_BASIC}\"\n        body: |\n          {\n            \"username\": \"${TAPIS_USERNAME}\",\n            \"password\": \"${TAPIS_PASSWORD}\",\n            \"grant_type\": \"password\"\n          }\n        conditions:\n          - \"[STATUS] == 200\"\n          - \"len([BODY].result.access_token.access_token) > 0\"\n        store:\n          tapis_token: \"[BODY].result.access_token.access_token\"\n\n      # 2) List actors with the minted token. Asserts shape + latency.\n      - name: list-actors\n        url: \"${TAPIS_BASE_URL}/v3/actors\"\n        method: GET\n        headers:\n          X-Tapis-Token: \"[CONTEXT].tapis_token\"\n        conditions:\n          - \"[STATUS] == 200\"\n          - \"[BODY].status == success\"\n          - \"[RESPONSE_TIME] < 2000\"\n\n      # 3) Paginated probe - a second GET to catch rapid list churn between runs.\n      - name: list-actors-paged\n        url: \"${TAPIS_BASE_URL}/v3/actors?limit=5\"\n        method: GET\n        headers:\n          X-Tapis-Token: \"[CONTEXT].tapis_token\"\n        conditions:\n          - \"[STATUS] == 200\"\n          - \"[BODY].status == success\"\n"
            }
          },
          "networking": {
            "default": {
              "protocol": "http",
              "port": 8080,
              "tapis_auth": true,
              "tapis_auth_allowed_users": [
                "*"
              ],
              "tapis_auth_return_path": "/",
              "tapis_ui_uri_redirect": true,
              "tapis_ui_uri_description": "Gatus - Tapis actors watch (postgres-backed, durable history)"
            }
          },
          "healthchecks": {
            "readiness": {
              "http_get_path": "/health",
              "http_get_port": 8080,
              "initial_delay_seconds": 5,
              "period_seconds": 10
            },
            "liveness": {
              "http_get_path": "/health",
              "http_get_port": 8080,
              "initial_delay_seconds": 30,
              "period_seconds": 15
            },
            "networking_requires_ready": true
          },
          "resources": {
            "cpu_request": 250,
            "cpu_limit": 1000,
            "mem_request": 256,
            "mem_limit": 1024
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "tag": "tapis-actors-postgres",
    "commit_message": "Gatus tapis-actors-suite + Postgres 17 (tapisvolume-backed) - in-suite X-Tapis-Token mint + 3-min /v3/actors watch, large durable history. Requires: TAPIS_USERNAME, TAPIS_PASSWORD, TAPIS_CLIENT_BASIC, and a Tapis volume ID.",
    "description": "Two-pod stack: internal-only Postgres 17 (on a tapisvolume) + gatus running the token-minting actors watch. storage.type: postgres with raised maximum-number-of-results/events gives a large history backlog that survives app restarts AND db-pod recreation. PG password auto-generated per stack; actor creds live only in pod env."
  }
}

docs {
  ## Gatus actors watch + Postgres (tapisvolume) - `tapis-actors-postgres`

  The "final" form of the actors watch: the `gatus:tapis-actors-suite` config
  (in-suite X-Tapis-Token mint -> 3-minute `/v3/actors` GET watch) re-homed onto
  the two-pod `db` + `app` postgres pattern, with retention raised for a large,
  durable history backlog.

  ### What it fixes vs `tapis-actors-suite`
  | | tapis-actors-suite | tapis-actors-postgres |
  |---|---|---|
  | storage | `memory` (wiped on restart) | `postgres` on a tapisvolume |
  | history | none across restarts | large backlog, survives app restart AND db recreation |
  | retention | n/a | `maximum-number-of-results: 10000`, `maximum-number-of-events: 1000` |

  ### Fill these at instantiation (from-template wizard)
  | key | required | what |
  |-----|----------|------|
  | `TAPIS_USERNAME` / `TAPIS_PASSWORD` | yes | user creds for the password grant (NOT a service account) |
  | `TAPIS_CLIENT_BASIC` | yes | base64(`client_id:client_key`) of a registered OAuth client |
  | db volume `source_id` | yes | a Tapis volume ID for `/var/lib/postgresql/data` |
  | `PG_PASSWORD` | auto | `${pods:random:32}`, generated once per stack |

  `TAPIS_BASE_URL` is a plain env literal (`https://tacc.tapis.io`) - edit the
  member env to point at another tenant.

  ### How much history is "large" here
  Retention is COUNT-based, not time-based: wall-clock per endpoint =
  `maximum-number-of-results x interval`. At the 3m suite cadence, 10000 results
  ~= **20.8 days** of per-result history per suite endpoint. Want more calendar
  coverage? Raise the suite `interval` (cheap) before raising the row cap (costs
  DB size + dashboard query time on every page load). Events (up/down
  transitions) are rare, so 1000 spans many months.

  ### Where the secrets live (env, not config)
  Unlike `gatus:tapis-postgres` (which fills `${pods:secrets:KEY}` into the
  rendered config for JWT/creds), this tag keeps the actor credentials in the
  pod ENV and lets gatus expand `${TAPIS_USERNAME}` / `${TAPIS_PASSWORD}` /
  `${TAPIS_CLIENT_BASIC}` at startup. So the stack secret_map carries them as
  `${:?...}` and the app member's `environment_variables` reference
  `${stack:secrets:...}` - the resolved values never land in the ConfigMap,
  only in the pod's k8s secret. The DB password takes the same env route
  (`GATUS_DB_*` + gatus `${VAR}` expansion) - `compile_member_stack_refs` walks
  env vars + secret_map but not `config_content`.

  ### Durability / ordering / networking
  - `db` mounts a **tapisvolume** at `/var/lib/postgresql/data`; `PGDATA` points
    at the `/pgdata` subdir so the mount root can hold `lost+found`. History now
    survives a full db-pod recreation, not just app restarts.
  - `ordered` + `depends_on: ["db"]` + `ready_condition: ready` => gatus starts
    only after `pg_isready -U gatus -d gatus` passes.
  - `db` is `local_only` (never routed by Traefik); only `app` gets a public,
    tapis_auth'd URL. `networking_requires_ready: true` holds the public URL
    behind the splash page until `/health` responds.

  ### Token endpoint caveat - client is required
  The Tapis password grant needs a registered OAuth client sent as a Basic auth
  header. An empty `TAPIS_CLIENT_BASIC` sends a malformed `Basic ` header and the
  endpoint returns 400. Create a client, then base64 its `client_id:client_key`:
  ```bash
  curl -H "X-Tapis-Token: $TOK" -d '{"client_id":"gatus-suite"}' \
    https://tacc.tapis.io/v3/oauth2/clients
  printf '%s' "gatus-suite:$CLIENT_KEY" | base64 -w0   # -> TAPIS_CLIENT_BASIC
  ```
}
